RISC-V: trust the calling convention for INT parameters (applies after perf-43).

The RISC-V psABI passes a 32-bit integer argument sign-extended to 64 bits (also an unsigned one),
and the JIT's callers keep to it: genPutArgReg sign-extends an INT argument unless
IsInt32SignExtendedInReg proves it already is, native code follows the psABI, and the runtime's stubs
pass argument registers through. perf-43 still sign-extended every register-homed INT parameter in
the prolog; it now does that only for a struct field mapped from a parameter register, whose upper
half the caller does not define.

Nethermind stateless guest on ZisK: steps -38,510 / -68,293 (-0.07% / -0.05%) and cost -2.76M /
-4.94M on blocks 26055159 / 26112793. Outputs identical on 11 mainnet blocks.

